# MCP docs design

Human inspiration pages in `mcp-docs/`. Runtime truth stays in `describe_capabilities` and gateway schemas — see [mcp-published-schemas.mdc](./mcp-published-schemas.mdc) for JSON sync.

Add a **section** when a miss repeats. Do not grow a mega-guide.

## Prompts

[PromptCard](mcp-docs/.vitepress/theme/components/PromptCard.vue) copies **only** the quote. `lookFor` stays on the page (not on the clipboard).

**Empty-chat test.** A pasted quote must work with no earlier message. If the quote says “this”, “these”, “my”, or “same” without naming the referent in that same sentence, rewrite it.

**Three kinds** — on EIP pages use group labels **Job**, **Lesson**, **Check**, **one** card each. Drop a kind when there is no honest example.

| Kind | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **Job** | The sentence a matching person would paste (wallet, deployer, integrator). |
| **Lesson** | Canonical contrast; both sides named in the quote (fork A vs B, self-send vs transfer). |
| **Check** | An old belief the lab should confirm or knock down, inputs inside the sentence. |

**Inputs in the quote.** Scenario txs need amount, recipient shape (empty / existing / self), and fork. Blocks name header fields when relevant. Opcodes: name a tiny program in words (`PUSH1 1 PUSH1 2 ADD`, DUPN at depth 4) — no long hex dumps. Precompiles: minimal vector in words (sizes + success question). Artifacts: generate then inspect in one sentence if needed — still no pasted JSON.

**Prose in the quote.** Paste text uses human words (prefund storage, paid gas, call gas, block header total) — not MCP/JSON field names (`gasUsed`, `accounts[]`, `txRegularGas`). `lookFor` on the page may stay technical for reviewers.

**Reuse.** [capabilities.md](mcp-docs/use/capabilities.md), [introduction.md](mcp-docs/use/introduction.md), and fork pages **reuse** the EIP sentence, not a vaguer twin. Tool-page openers that already pass the test stay.

**Live voice.** Do not write “once the public MCP is live” — point at [Connect](/use/connect) as open now.

## Catalogue pages

Per-EIP pages are twins of explorations — identity and spec pins follow [eip-canonical-data.mdc](./eip-canonical-data.mdc). Do not duplicate long probe tables; link tools and schemas.
